  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Johns Hopkins University Applied Physics Laboratory recorded $1.9B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date across 822 awards, with an average award size of $2.3M. Obligations are down 18.6% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer at $1.4B, followed by the National Aeronautics and Space Administration at $497M. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) is the dominant market at $1.7B. FY21 through FY25 totals show a rising trend into FY25 before the partial FY26 total: FY21 was $1.5B, FY22 was $1.6B, FY23 was $2B, FY24 was $2B, and FY25 was $2.4B. Current-year totals are partial because the period covers fiscal year to date. Award counts, average sizes, and the concentration in a few large buyers and a single dominant NAICS explain how obligations accumulate in the partial FY26 reporting window.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "?Who are the biggest buyers of Johns Hopkins University Applied Physics Laboratory in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $1.4B. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $497M. The Department of Homeland Security, Department of Health and Human Services, Department of Commerce, Department of Transportation, Department of State, and Department of Energy together account for the remaining obligations at $27.7M, $10.2M, $4.2M, $2.7M, $1.1M, and $472K respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "?Which markets drive Johns Hopkins University Applied Physics Laboratory federal revenue in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) accounts for $1.7B. Engineering Services and All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services follow at $89.9M and $76.4M. Smaller markets include Other Computer Related Services at $38.6M and Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing at $7.5M, among others."
      }
    ]
  },
